// Oracle batch 104 (task 0328): the world's ported VU1 micro programs (tfrag A / B, tie A / B, shrub A / B:
// assets/generated/src/game/ovl/world_vu1_*.cpp, generated by tools/codegen/gen_world_vu.py from tools/codegen/vu2cpp.py) against the VU
// interpreter running the uploaded original, on the start states the programs have in the running game
// (rac1-native with RAC1_VU1_CAPTURE=<dir> RAC1_VU1_CAPTURE_ALL=<n>: assets/dumps/oracle/vu1_world/{veldin_play,veldin_intro,
// novalis,kerwan}, generated, not in the repo).
//  - world_vu1_exact: the exact step-by-step ports in lockstep with the interpreter (every register, the flags, the
//    pc after every instruction; data memory every 64 steps; the XGKICK packets), as batch 79 does for the mobys;
//  - world_vu1_fast: the fast ports (basic blocks), as batch 95 does for the mobys: the interpreter runs exactly as
//    many instructions as the port reports, the whole state compared after each call and at the end, the kicks.
// Each state is run as captured and with perturbed floats / registers / memory (other clipping, lighting, loop
// paths). The micro memory comes from each file (the set that was loaded when the program started); a state whose
// micro memory does not hold one of the six programs (another pass's code) is skipped.
// ORACLE_VU1_DIR=a:b more / other directories; ORACLE_SEED; ORACLE_VU1_VARIANTS; ORACLE_COVER=1 lists the micro
// addresses of each program no case ran; ORACLE_WORLD_PROGRAM=<name> only one program.

